WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:03.259
Hello, and welcome one and all to Wonder Vision!

00:00:03.259 --> 00:00:07.470
No, not that one, although we can understand
the confusion.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:12.660
This is no superhero sitcom though; this is
the latest innovation from our dear friend

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:13.660
Doctor Wondertainment.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:19.110
Tell me, have you ever wondered who would
win in a fight between, let’s say, Superman

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:20.110
and Goku?

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:22.230
Is that pairing a little too by the numbers?

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:30.010
Okay, how about something more like this:
Godzilla vs SCP-5514, aka The Dragonslayer,

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:36.370
a giant mech suit designed by the SCP Foundation
for the sole purpose of taking on giant city-destroying

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:39.750
creatures like the old King of the Monsters
himself.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.340
Now, that’s more like it!

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:46.149
And scenarios just like that are exactly what
we’re here for!

00:00:46.149 --> 00:00:50.420
Friends, we’ve all spent so much time pondering
the ‘what ifs’, but as much as it would

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:54.579
be a fun use of our time, we can’t all spend
our days daydreaming.

00:00:54.579 --> 00:01:00.300
Luckily though, Doctor Wondertainment has
just the thing that we need; how does he do

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.300
it?

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:06.049
Introducing his newest and perhaps his most
ingenious creation yet: Wonder Vision.

00:01:06.049 --> 00:01:10.920
Through the miracle of the good doctor’s
patented and highly secret technology, you

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:16.280
can now experience the outcomes of any fictitious
situation you can possibly think up!

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:19.029
And all from the comfort of your own home.

00:01:19.029 --> 00:01:24.270
Why waste hours daydreaming, let Wonder Vision
do all the imagining so you don’t have to!

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.340
So, are you ready to take it for a spin?

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:32.599
Oh, of course, there are so many possibilities,
so many scenarios to think up, it can leave

00:01:32.599 --> 00:01:35.849
you feeling a little bit spoilt for choice,
can’t it?

00:01:35.849 --> 00:01:39.270
Tell you what, start with a fight scenario
those are always good!

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:44.219
An old fashioned one on one grudge match;
after all, who hasn’t wanted to see two

00:01:44.219 --> 00:01:48.310
things that would never normally face off
with each other go toe to toe?

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:50.569
Here, you input the first fighter…

00:01:50.569 --> 00:01:53.119
SCP-682, a popular choice!

00:01:53.119 --> 00:01:57.849
The Hard to Destroy Reptile, infamously on
of the most fearsome and tenacious anomalies

00:01:57.849 --> 00:02:00.549
ever encountered by the SCP Foundation.

00:02:00.549 --> 00:02:04.850
Whoever you’re going to be pitting against
it definitely has their work cut out for them.

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:08.009
Now, you could pick out another SCP to fight
your first candidate.

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:12.599
But why not try something different, really
push the boat out.

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:15.620
After all, with Wonder Vision, anything is
possible!

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:18.860
So, come on, introducing your next contender…

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:19.860
Deadpool!

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.760
Ah, a comic book fan, are we?

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:26.239
Well, once again you’ve hit on an interesting
choice.

00:02:26.239 --> 00:02:30.819
Also known as Wade Wilson, this Canadian mutant
from Marvel Comics is not only a master of

00:02:30.819 --> 00:02:37.159
martial arts and almost every form of combat,
but much like your friend SCP-682, he’s

00:02:37.159 --> 00:02:40.909
got a knack for healing even the worst injuries
imaginable.

00:02:40.909 --> 00:02:42.900
This one is going to be close…

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.780
it also might take a while.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:45.780
“Oh, hey there.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:47.660
What is this, someone’s YouTube video?

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:48.780
Better watch my swears!”

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:50.719
So, let’s get started with your match-up!

00:02:50.719 --> 00:02:55.290
Combatants, take your places, it’s time
for round one!

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:56.290
“Combatants?

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:58.659
Wait a minute, am I on Battleworld right now?

00:02:58.659 --> 00:03:00.709
No wait, it’s Mojoworld right?

00:03:00.709 --> 00:03:04.909
Okay, maybe some other ‘world’ obsessed
with one on one gladiatorial arena fights.

00:03:04.909 --> 00:03:05.909
Is this the UFC?

00:03:05.909 --> 00:03:07.420
Also, another question…

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.959
what the hell is that big angry-looking lizard?”

00:03:09.959 --> 00:03:13.760
Here we go, Wonder Vision is now generating
every possible outcome.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.480
Let’s take a look at this scenario!

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:20.909
Now, we all know that SCP-682 has always been
a formidable foe, and one of its attributes

00:03:20.909 --> 00:03:23.870
that makes its so fearsome is its size.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:29.400
The Hard to Destroy Reptile is an unambiguous
monster, a large quadrupedal creature sporting

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:36.370
two pairs of legs, a tail and a vaguely crocodilian
head, its mouth filled with razor sharp teeth.

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:40.969
But as the old adage goes, the bigger they
are, the harder they fall.

00:03:40.969 --> 00:03:45.900
And nobody knows better about using an opponent’s
size to his advantage than the Merc with the

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:46.900
Mouth.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:49.049
“You can say that again, Mr Narrator Guy!

00:03:49.049 --> 00:03:51.980
Hey, do I really have to fight this killer
croc over here?

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:53.819
Oops, sorry, wrong universe.”

00:03:53.819 --> 00:03:57.849
On top of that, good old Deadpool is one of
the most highly skilled swordsmen in the entire

00:03:57.849 --> 00:04:02.650
Marvel Universe, rivaled only by the likes
of Wolverine, Taskmaster and Blade.

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:07.439
It’s a pretty well-known fact that those
dual-katanas of his aren’t just for show!

00:04:07.439 --> 00:04:11.019
“Call it overcompensating, I dare you!”

00:04:11.019 --> 00:04:15.980
His training and tactics already put our underdog
Wade W. Wilson at a little bit of an advantage.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:20.620
But let’s not forget, SCP-682 is no slouch
either.

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:25.530
The reptile is known to be pretty fast when
it needs to be, fueled by its own sheer hatred

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:27.810
for all other forms of life.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:32.920
That’s its motivation, the sole driving
force behind the creature; it thinks of anything

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:35.350
else as an abomination.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:41.130
Whether it be a person or a plant, even other
anomalies, every living thing other than itself

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:47.630
are unforgivable, unnatural and disgusting
to SCP-682, and it will stop at nothing to

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:49.979
kill anything it sees.

00:04:49.979 --> 00:04:55.220
Of course, that’s a little tricky when the
only person nearby is a mutant with a similar

00:04:55.220 --> 00:05:00.340
penchant for bodily regeneration, as well
as notoriously big mouth.

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:04.889
As fast as the Hard to Destroy Reptile can
be, it is hindered, its own slightly larger

00:05:04.889 --> 00:05:07.280
size can make the creature cumbersome.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:11.630
It isn’t by much, but it’s just enough
for our old pal Deadpool to get to work doing

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:13.169
what he does best.

00:05:13.169 --> 00:05:18.949
Unsheathing his pair of pristine swords, Wade
flies into battle as gung-ho as ever.

00:05:18.949 --> 00:05:24.970
He lands the first blow, lodging one of his
blades in SCP-682 reptilian musculature.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:29.520
The reptile lets out a furious roar, one that
would strike fear into anybody else.

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:30.520
But Deadpool?

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:36.190
Well, he’s not exactly the fearful type;
more the too insane to back down type.

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:40.599
Now the Hard to Destroy Reptile’s hide is
pretty thick, usually providing it with enough

00:05:40.599 --> 00:05:45.940
protective layers to defend the creature against
most conventional forms of attack; guns, bombs,

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:49.300
knives or, in this case, swords.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:55.479
But the adaptability and resistance of SCP-682
is only matched by Deadpool’s resourcefulness

00:05:55.479 --> 00:05:58.820
– also his reckless and wildly unpredictable
nature.

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:04.289
But speaking of resourceful, his swords – sometimes
known as Bea and Arthur – aren’t forged

00:06:04.289 --> 00:06:06.259
from any ordinary metal.

00:06:06.259 --> 00:06:10.920
Wily old Wade Wilson has been known to wield
katana’s made out of Carbonadium, a metal

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:16.199
that can not only deflect powerful incoming
attacks, but the element itself is also able

00:06:16.199 --> 00:06:21.450
to disrupt the healing factor of certain mutants,
like Wolverine.

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:26.980
The sharpened Carbonadium slices through the
scaly, leathery hide of SCP-682, much to the

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:29.810
reptile’s disgust and annoyance.

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:35.460
It moves to retaliate, swiping at the mutant
mercenary with its claws, each as sharp as

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:37.830
the blades of Deadpool’s weapons.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:43.370
His natural reflexes kick in, slightly enhanced
by the process that triggered his mutation

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:45.850
and his rigorous special ops training.

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:50.160
Deadpool blocks the oncoming attack by crossing
both swords above his head, but the force

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:53.460
behind SCP-682’s blow staggers him.

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:58.280
You see, he might be slightly faster than
the life-hating lizard thanks to his smaller

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:03.390
size, but Deadpool simply doesn’t possess
the same muscle mass and bodily strength as

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:05.000
a gigantic monster.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:07.350
But he can still hold his own.

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:09.970
“Hey, watch that cheeky double entendre
there, Mr Narrator.

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:11.770
God, this gecko is jacked.”

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:17.770
Deploying a spin manoeuvre, guiding the heavy
limb of SCP-682 over his head, Deadpool uses

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:23.349
his katanas like a pair of giant Carbonadium
scissors - A move that would make Able proud.

00:07:23.349 --> 00:07:27.700
He cleaves off one of the monster’s arms,
slicing through the thick hide into the muscle

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:33.970
and bone beneath, causing the creature to
lose its footing, tumbling forward over itself.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:39.370
Using the beast’s fall to his advantage,
Deadpool leaps onto 682’s back.

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:43.670
Raising his two swords, he plunges the blades
into the crocodilian head of the monster,

00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:46.389
each one stabbing directly through its skull.

00:07:46.389 --> 00:07:50.969
Sprays of blood, brains and viscera spew from
the wound, not that you can tell from the

00:07:50.969 --> 00:07:54.610
state of Deadpool’s suit; that’s why he
wears red, after all.

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:57.860
“You joke, but do you have any idea how
hard this is gonna be to wash out?

00:07:57.860 --> 00:08:03.110
I’m talking tide pends, seltzer water and
lemon, I swear if any of these stains set

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:04.110
in…”

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:07.340
Unfortunately, Deadpool does have a penchant
for getting distracted.

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:11.319
Partly fighting back out of aggression, and
possibly partly due to finding the motormouthed

00:08:11.319 --> 00:08:17.280
mutant to be a bit of a nuisance, SCP-682
quickly rolls over onto its back.

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:21.860
Startled by the sudden movement, Deadpool
loses his balance and falls to the ground,

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:26.969
quickly followed by the full weight of a giant,
Hard to Destroy Reptile; like we said, the

00:08:26.969 --> 00:08:29.560
bigger they are, the harder they fall.

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:33.870
Pinned under the beast, Wade reaches for Bea,
trying to use the sword as a makeshift crutch

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:35.520
to pull himself free.

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:38.080
“Hey, I’m down but not out!

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:40.680
Let me in, coach, I’ll bite his scaly ankles
off!”

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:45.760
Back on his two feet, and finding himself
facing an enemy back on four, Deadpool opts

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:48.020
for a more scorched earth approach.

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:50.820
It’s time for scenario two.

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:55.270
Few people know this about our dear friend
Mr Wilson, but he actually has more than a

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:59.690
few tricks up his blood-stained sleeves; or
rather, in his magic satchel.

00:08:59.690 --> 00:09:04.340
Yes, you heard that right, the equipment bag
Deadpool is normally seen wearing has its

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:06.950
own extranormal properties to it.

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:11.450
The satchel itself contains a near infinite
pocket dimension, along with the ability to

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:14.460
create anything that the user needs.

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:18.610
Extra ammo, replacement swords, and endless
supply of stuffed unicorns…

00:09:18.610 --> 00:09:19.610
“Hey!

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:20.780
How did you know about those?”

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:24.470
You name it and Deadpool can produce it from
his bag in a matter of seconds.

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:28.880
Again, we really need to get this guy and
Able to hang out sometime, don’t we?

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:33.230
Say what you will about the speed and ferocity
of one of the Foundation’s most notorious

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:37.610
anomalies, but no reptile has an abundance
of extra hardware in its pocket.

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:39.780
“You know, that’s not a bad idea.

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:42.560
I mean I’m not just doing this because you
said I would…

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:43.950
or who knows, maybe I am?

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:44.950
Hey, croc!

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:46.290
I hope you like pineapple!”

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:50.420
With that, Deadpool unleashed a volley of
grenades, all pulled from the extradimensional

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:53.950
satchel and launched straight at SCP-682.

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:59.470
The ensuing explosions are deafening, engulfing
the Hard to Destroy Reptile and the area around

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:01.820
it in flames and debris.

00:10:01.820 --> 00:10:06.220
“Lucky the writers let me have my bag with
me, I honestly don’t think I’d stand a

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:07.840
fighting chance without it!”

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:13.710
Unfortunately, as we mentioned earlier, SCP-682
is pretty thick skinned, able to resist a

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:17.530
lot of the explosive punishment Deadpool is
dealing out.

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:21.930
Conventional weapons, even combustible materials
and ordinance, do little to cause the creature

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:26.210
any lasting harm, and mainly serve to anger
the reptile even further.

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:28.400
“Oh, come on, man!

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:30.420
What about if I use this?”

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:35.150
Pulling a bazooka from his magical satchel,
Deadpool launches the most destructive, expensive,

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:40.570
and excessive explosive he can think of: a
diamond tipped, high velocity, heat seeking

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:41.570
warhead.

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:46.520
The missile lets loose, piercing the outer
layer of SCP-682’s scales and lodges itself

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:52.150
deep in its side as the creature turns to
deflect the full force of the oncoming ordinance.

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:56.320
The reptile roars in pain and aggression to
feel the super dense tip of the projectile

00:10:56.320 --> 00:11:01.520
burrowing into it, through its thick, defensive
exterior and into its flesh.

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:04.680
You might want to cover your ears for what
follows.

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:06.990
“Hey, stop addressing the audience, that’s
my bit!

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:09.310
Wait, what was that about covering ears?”

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:15.120
With an almighty boom, the warhead detonates,
spewing flame and chunks of charred SCP-682

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:17.250
in every conceivable direction.

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:22.730
Smoke fills the space around them, as the
monstrous creature hisses in contempt, thrashing

00:11:22.730 --> 00:11:23.730
in pain.

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:27.110
Suddenly, a large, scale-covered tail whips
out of the smoke.

00:11:27.110 --> 00:11:31.520
Still suffering from a nasty bout of military
grade tinnitus from the blast, Deadpool looks

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:38.270
up only too late as powerful appendage swipes
at him, sending the Merc with the Mouth reeling;

00:11:38.270 --> 00:11:41.070
SCP-692 is far from dead.

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:45.600
As the fumes from the detonation clear, its
smouldering wound is already starting to heal.

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:48.210
But that gives Deadpool an idea.

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:51.760
Reaching into his magic satchel, Wade fishes
out another grenade.

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:56.740
The moment his gloved had grabs it, another
roar fills the area; the Hard to Destroy Reptile

00:11:56.740 --> 00:12:01.390
begins barrelling towards the regenerating
mutant in red, baring its wide maw of sharp

00:12:01.390 --> 00:12:02.390
teeth.

00:12:02.390 --> 00:12:04.440
“Well, this is a terrible idea.”

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:08.910
Pulling out a fresh grenade, Deadpool charges
directly towards the oncoming reptile, wrenching

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:12.790
the pin from the handheld explosive and flicking
free the safety handle.

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:17.750
He leaps up into the air, aiming to achieve
a balletic flip over the head of the angry

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:18.750
monster.

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:25.240
With its tenacious and loudmouthed prey in
mid air above it, SCP-682 lifts its jaws upwards,

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:30.680
just as Deadpool turns to drop the primed
grenade in the Hard to Destroy Reptile’s

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:31.680
mouth.

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:35.890
This goes about as well as you’d expect;
Deadpool is caught right between the large,

00:12:35.890 --> 00:12:38.850
crocodilian jaws of SCP-682.

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:43.240
The monstrous anomaly plucks the acrobatic
assassin out of the air with ease, But, in

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:48.440
his hand, he’s still got the grenade, and
its timer is rapidly ticking down.

00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:54.080
Another in a series of huge, deafening explosions
rips through the head of SCP-682 before the

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:57.700
reptile has a chance to swallow Deadpool and
his grenade.

00:12:57.700 --> 00:13:02.060
Thanks in equal parts to the sharp teeth tearing
him apart, as well as the blast of his own

00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:05.760
grenade, there’s not much remaining of Deadpool
that’s still alive.

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:07.770
“No, I’m fine, really!

00:13:07.770 --> 00:13:11.230
Just give me a few hours to grow back my entire
body.

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:13.540
Actually, could someone come and pick my head
up?

00:13:13.540 --> 00:13:14.540
No?

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:17.330
That’s okay, I’ll just… roll, I guess.”

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:21.680
Well, technically Deadpool is still alive,
thanks to his mutation.

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:28.030
Much like his opponent SCP-682 here, his regenerative
healing is so effective he can continue to

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:33.950
function even when the rest of his body – skeleton,
nervous system, internal organs – is completely

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:34.950
obliterated.

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:38.510
Then again, just blowing off the Hard to Destroy
Reptile’s head is only enough to temporarily

00:13:38.510 --> 00:13:43.090
slow it down, this is the same creature that
survived being cut in half by a laser, and

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:47.060
having its neck snapped repeatedly over ten
hours by SCP-173.

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:51.020
So, while these two are gradually reconstituting
themselves…

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:54.920
again, why don’t we chalk this one up to
a tie?

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:56.250
“A tie?

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:57.280
Come on, man!

00:13:57.280 --> 00:14:02.120
Hey, I’m still – wait for it, wait for
it – ‘a head’ of the competition!

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:03.120
Anyone?

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:05.710
Yeesh, rough crowd.”

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:10.040
Let’s just jump ahead a few hours, give
these two a chance to heal up.

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:14.670
Now, by this point our old pal Deadpool has
used most of his go-to options for a fight,

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:19.170
and they’re not exactly proving to be all
too effective against SCP-682.

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:22.280
“Hey, I’m doing my best here!”

00:14:22.280 --> 00:14:26.530
The Hard to Destroy Reptile, on the other
hand, is still fresh for a fight, as extensively

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:29.660
healing itself rarely tires the creature out.

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:34.911
Combine that with a rage that just won’t
be quelled, and an opponent who isn’t just

00:14:34.911 --> 00:14:39.790
another form of life, but another living being
who also can’t be killed without regenerating,

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:44.970
and that all adds up to one very angry lizard
and not a lot of other options for Deadpool.

00:14:44.970 --> 00:14:45.970
“Other options, huh?

00:14:45.970 --> 00:14:49.250
Okay, I can think of a few.”

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:51.070
With that, Deadpool vanishes.

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:54.080
Just like that, in the blink of an eye, he’s
gone.

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:58.360
It's not unprecedented for him, after all
he does possess a particular piece of technology

00:14:58.360 --> 00:15:00.270
that allows him to do this.

00:15:00.270 --> 00:15:04.580
Deadpool has been known to sometimes wear
a teleportation bracelet, a device created

00:15:04.580 --> 00:15:08.380
by his friend and go-to for gadgets, Weasel.

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:11.760
As to exactly where he’s gone to, that’s
anyone’s guess.

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:17.680
It’s a bold strategy, just trying to outrun
SCP-682 instead of facing it, but admittedly

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:19.490
a little unexpected from…

00:15:19.490 --> 00:15:21.870
“Ta-da, okay, I’m back!

00:15:21.870 --> 00:15:23.460
And I brought new toys!”

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:28.280
In an astounding and completely baffling move,
Deadpool teleports right back to where he

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:29.750
was just standing.

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:36.640
Brandishing a golden glove with six shining
gemstones encrusted in it: the Infinity Gauntlet.

00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:43.510
SCP-682 seems to know what this artefact is,
or is at least wary of it, and keeps its distance.

00:15:43.510 --> 00:15:47.130
“Bet you weren’t expecting this, later
gator!”

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:52.530
Acting with a reckless abandon typical of
nobody other than him, Wade snaps his fingers.

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:56.620
Historically, only beings of immense power
are able to wield the Infinity Gauntlet and

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:57.620
survive.

00:15:57.620 --> 00:16:02.100
The cosmically-powerful metal glove is designed
to combine the effects of the six Infinity

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:08.270
Gems, each one governing a different aspect
of existence – namely time, space, reality,

00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:10.980
power, the mind and the soul.

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:16.230
As Deadpool’s fingers click, SCP-682 is
wiped from existence, turned into nothing

00:16:16.230 --> 00:16:19.520
more than a pile of dust floating through
the air.

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:23.890
Unfortunately for Wade wielding it, the Gauntlet’s
cosmic energy is so uncontainable that it

00:16:23.890 --> 00:16:27.320
is channelled back at him, almost obliterating
him entirely.

00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:29.090
“Worth it, though.

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:31.180
Let’s see Brolin top that.”

00:16:31.180 --> 00:16:35.260
To make matters worse, SCP-682 isn’t down
for long.

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:40.040
While Deadpool’s own healing factor is struggling
to restore him, the Hard to Destroy Reptile

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:45.390
is rapidly reconstituting itself, knitting
its physical form back into existence on a

00:16:45.390 --> 00:16:49.190
cellular level, fueled by sheer hatred and
willpower.

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:53.630
Rummaging through the small collection of
objects he brought back with him when he returned,

00:16:53.630 --> 00:16:56.600
Deadpool slips a metal helmet onto his head.

00:16:56.600 --> 00:17:01.870
This is no ordinary helmet though, it’s
Cerebro, a powerful device used by Professor

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:07.459
Charles Xavier, a powerful psychic that uses
the helmet to amplify his powers and find

00:17:07.459 --> 00:17:08.939
fellow mutants.

00:17:08.939 --> 00:17:12.230
Although quite what Wade has planed for it
is anyone’s guess.

00:17:12.230 --> 00:17:14.289
“Oh, well I’m glad you asked!

00:17:14.289 --> 00:17:18.529
I’m technically brain dead, so I figured
I could use this doohickie to connect my mind

00:17:18.529 --> 00:17:20.260
to the big nasty lizard over there.

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:24.649
Then, I can project my own brain death into
him and finally put an end to this wild ride.”

00:17:24.649 --> 00:17:29.830
While it’s indeed an interesting plan, there
are unfortunately some pitfalls of Deadpool’s

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:31.000
latest tactic.

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:35.909
One being that only incredibly powerful psychics
like Professor X, Jean Grey, or Emma Frost

00:17:35.909 --> 00:17:38.720
can even attempt to connect their mind to
Cerebro.

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:44.299
The other snare in the plan is, that’s not
how Cerebro works at all, it’s for tracking

00:17:44.299 --> 00:17:47.840
mutants, not projecting someone’s consciousness
into the mind of another.

00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:52.120
“Oh, come on, I’ve been fighting this
lizard, with you semi-sarcastically chastising,

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:53.639
me all afternoon.

00:17:53.639 --> 00:17:55.020
Cut me a break here!

00:17:55.020 --> 00:17:59.970
All I have left is this little whatchamacallit
that I stole from that stretchy Poindexter.”

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:05.409
With SCP-682 once again baring down on him,
Deadpool aimlessly fires the weapon.

00:18:05.409 --> 00:18:09.660
Unbeknownst to him, the device he’s currently
holding is the Ultimate Nullifier, the most

00:18:09.660 --> 00:18:12.580
devastating weapon in the entire universe.

00:18:12.580 --> 00:18:18.860
The blast from the Nullifier envelops SCP-682,
completely and utterly eliminating it, violating

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:21.510
the very law of conservation of mass.

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:23.289
“Hey, what do you know, it worked!

00:18:23.289 --> 00:18:24.409
Say, can I go now?

00:18:24.409 --> 00:18:25.720
Wow, this thing is getting hot…

00:18:25.720 --> 00:18:27.299
oh, look, a penny!”

00:18:27.299 --> 00:18:31.559
One downside of using the Ultimate Nullifier
is that it can often backfire, completely

00:18:31.559 --> 00:18:36.559
destroying the person wielding it too, especially
if their mind isn’t strong enough... or

00:18:36.559 --> 00:18:38.200
if they lose focus.

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:41.230
And well, sadly Deadpool has a knack for getting
distracted.

00:18:41.230 --> 00:18:46.830
While the Nullifier continues to obliterate
both its target, SCP-682, and its wielder,

00:18:46.830 --> 00:18:51.039
Deadpool, its power destroys the entire universe
from beginning to end.

00:18:51.039 --> 00:18:55.800
This power continues until it is the only
thing left in existence, only to then collapse

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:57.870
back on itself.

00:18:57.870 --> 00:19:02.629
The Ultimate Nullifier ends up paradoxically
nullifying its own effect, ultimately then

00:19:02.629 --> 00:19:07.970
recreating the universe in the blink of an
eye, including Deadpool and SCP-682.

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:11.580
So, we guess that’s another tie?

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:13.299
“Oh, come on!”

00:19:13.299 --> 00:19:19.919
Now go and check out “SCP-096 VS SCP-173”
to see the outcome of another chaotic clash

00:19:19.919 --> 00:19:22.110
between the Shy Guy and The Sculpture.

00:19:22.110 --> 00:19:27.570
Or, for more tips on how to take down a certain
regenerating reptile, go and watch “WAS

00:19:27.570 --> 00:19:29.820
SCP-682 REALLY THAT HARD TO KILL AFTER ALL?”

